		<item>
		<title>New Zealand hits Russian oil shadow fleet with 65 new sanctions after insurer scandal</title>
		<link>https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/10/31/new-zealand-hits-russian-oil-shadow-fleet-with-65-new-sanctions-after-insurer-scandal/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Maria Tril]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Fri, 31 Oct 2025 19:03:58 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Latest news Ukraine]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[New Zealand]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Russian invasion]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Russian oil]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[shadow fleet]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Ukraine]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://euromaidanpress.com/?p=370896</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[Days after Reuters revealed a New Zealand insurer facilitated tens of billions in sanctioned oil trade, Wellington announced Thursday it is sanctioning 65 shadow fleet vessels and actors from Belarus, Iran and North Korea involved in Russian oil operations.]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img width="1024" height="576" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/russian-shadow-fleet-tanker-eagle-s-detained-by-finland-for-submarine-cable-sabotage-1024x576.jpg" class="attachment-large size-large wp-post-image" alt="Russian shadow fleet&#039;s tanker Eagle S, detained by the Finnish police." decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/russian-shadow-fleet-tanker-eagle-s-detained-by-finland-for-submarine-cable-sabotage-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/russian-shadow-fleet-tanker-eagle-s-detained-by-finland-for-submarine-cable-sabotage-300x169.jpg 300w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/russian-shadow-fleet-tanker-eagle-s-detained-by-finland-for-submarine-cable-sabotage-380x214.jpg 380w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/russian-shadow-fleet-tanker-eagle-s-detained-by-finland-for-submarine-cable-sabotage-800x450.jpg 800w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/russian-shadow-fleet-tanker-eagle-s-detained-by-finland-for-submarine-cable-sabotage-1160x653.jpg 1160w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/russian-shadow-fleet-tanker-eagle-s-detained-by-finland-for-submarine-cable-sabotage.jpg 1200w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></p><div data-type="_mgwidget" data-widget-id="1845881"></div>        
        <script>
            (function(w,q){w[q]=w[q]||[];w[q].push(["_mgc.load"])})(window,"_mgq");
        </script>
    
<p>New Zealand announced on 30 October it is imposing sanctions on 65 additional shadow fleet vessels and seven entities connected to Russia's oil trade, along with two individuals from Belarus, Iran and North Korea involved in refining and transporting Russian oil.</p>



<p>Foreign Minister Winston Peters made the announcement during meetings with Nordic 5 foreign ministers in Stockholm. The sanctions target actors "part of a broader network enabling the trade in Russian oil, undermining global efforts to curtail funding for Russia's illegal war," Peters <a href="https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/new-zealand-targets-shadow-fleet-expanded-russia-sanctions-2025-10-29/">said </a>in a statement.</p>



<p>The shadow fleet consists of tankers that transport sanctioned cargoes from countries including Iran, Russia and Venezuela while concealing their operations through fake locations, documents and vessel names.</p><div data-fuse="incontent_1"></div>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p><em>"By targeting the oil supply chain, New Zealand is acting decisively in support of international efforts to bring Russia to the negotiating table,"</em> Peters said.</p>
</blockquote>



<p>The timing follows Reuters reporting Tuesday that Maritime Mutual, a small insurer based in New Zealand, had facilitated trade worth tens of billions of dollars in Iranian and Russian oil by providing insurance to vessels evading Western sanctions. The coverage enables these ships to enter ports that require proof of insurance.</p>



<p>The sanctions expand New Zealand's measures against Russia's energy sector, specifically targeting the financial mechanisms and transportation networks that allow sanctioned oil to reach global markets.</p>


